# Line endings are checked out LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Two things break on a CRLF checkout of this repo:
#
#   - src/cli/index.js is a `bin` entry, so its shebang must end in a bare \n.
#     A published `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` makes `npx report-studio` fail with
#     `env: node\r: No such file or directory` on macOS and Linux. Vite's own
#     hashbang strip is /^#!.*\n/, so under CRLF it leaves the `#!` in place and
#     every spec that imports the CLI dies with a bare SyntaxError.
#   - test/styles.test.js matches multi-line CSS selectors as literal text.
#
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
